{"name":"Butterscotch Mousse","hex":"#a97d54","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butterscotch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard candy made from butter, brown sugar, syrup and vanilla.","A sauce or syrup made of similar ingredients."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown colour, like that of butterscotch candy.","Having the flavour of butterscotch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butterscotch"},{"term":"mousse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An airy pudding served chilled, particularly chocolate mousse.","A savory dish, of meat or seafood, containing gelatin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply mousse (styling cream)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mousse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butterscotch","blocks":[{"text":"Butterscotch is a type of confection whose primary ingredients are brown sugar and butter. Some recipes include cream, vanilla, and salt. The earliest known recipes, in mid-19th century Yorkshire, used treacle (molasses) in place of, or in addition to, sugar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Butterscotch-Candies.jpg/330px-Butterscotch-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butterscotch"},{"title":"Mousse","blocks":[{"text":"A mousse is a soft, prepared food that incorporates air bubbles to give it a light and airy texture. It can range from light and fluffy to creamy and thick. A mousse may be sweet or savory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Chocolate_coffee_mousse.jpg/330px-Chocolate_coffee_mousse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mousse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg/500px-Rye_%2815045370394%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par